   "purpose": "Resolve the runtime uncertainties in review_status before any scientific evaluation: show that each recorded episode is exactly 1000 consecutive post-physics samples, that the final sample is the actual terminal transition, that no reset state enters the trajectory, and that the effective robot-ground friction equals the cell; and measure wall time per run.",
   "exit_criteria": [
    "exit code 0; header completed true; footer verifies (verify_written and read_run report no problems)",
    "sync_checks.ok true with samples_checked = 128 x 1000 and every counter zero: capture_length_not_consecutive, termination_flag_mismatch, done_without_reset_after_capture, state_changed_after_capture, command_mismatch, steps_without_physics_advance",
    "sync_checks.reset_episode_length_max = 0 (the collector's reset took effect before the first recorded step); terminal_steps = [1000]; reset_moved_robot = 128 (each reset happened after, and outside, the recorded terminal sample)",
    "episode lengths min = max = 1000; unexpected_early_dones = 0",
    "runtime_checks.ok true: active terminations ['time_out']; no removed event active; robot shape friction readback 0.8 / 0.6; motor lag 0, strength 1.0",
    "runtime_checks.contact: every ground material and robot collision material listed with its combine mode; effective_static = [0.8], effective_dynamic = [0.6]; robot and ground share no material; no unbound robot collision shape",
    "measured wall time per run recorded"
   ],
   "note": "Smoke output is kept but never analysed or pooled.",
   "on_failure": "No scientific run. The output file (sync failure, exit 3) or <out>.diagnostic.json (runtime check failure) is reviewed, the cause is fixed in a new collector revision, and S0 is re-authorized."
